To solve $f(f(f(2)))$ when $f(x) = 5x-4$, we follow the steps:

1. First, we find $f(2)$:
\begin{align*}
f(2) &= 5(2) - 4 \\
&= 10 - 4 \\
&= 6.
\end{align*}

2. Next, we find $f(f(2))$ which is $f(6)$:
\begin{align*}
f(6) &= 5(6) - 4 \\
&= 30 - 4 \\
&= 26.
\end{align*}

3. Finally, we find $f(f(f(2)))$ which is $f(26)$:
\begin{align*}
f(26) &= 5(26) - 4 \\
&= 130 - 4 \\
&= 126.
\end{align*}

Therefore, $f(f(f(2))) = \boxed{126}$.

