problem:
Given the following function for population dynamics, determine the value of \( x \) when \( p = 0.6 \).

\[ 
x(p)=\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
1, \text { if } 0 \leq p \leq \frac{1}{2} \\
\frac{q}{p}, \text { if } \frac{1}{2}<p \leq 1 
\end{array}
\right.
\]

In this context, \( p = 0.6 > \frac{1}{2} \), thus \( x = \frac{q}{p} = \frac{2}{3} \).
